=== REASONING ===
Why the design preserves ADR-015 and P1-P10:

I1 default-off:
  Registry entry DefaultOn:false. The aigen-regenerated
  web/src/ai/features.ts reflects DefaultOn:false. New users land
  with the feature toggle off; only an explicit operator opt-in
  surfaces the AI panel.

I3 baseline intact:
  AIMqttSseInspectorExplanations renders BELOW the Connection
  Info GlassPanel and ABOVE the Throughput Chart. Every existing
  baseline section (4 StatCards, Connection Info, Throughput
  Chart, Vehicle Breakdown DataTable, stale-counter chip)
  renders unchanged with identical props. The off-mode test
  TestMqttSseInspectorAIOffShowsRawInspectorOnly mounts the
  full MQTTInspectorPage with ai_mode='off' and asserts the
  broker hostname, topic pattern, vehicle count, and AI surface
  ABSENCE are all simultaneously true — proving the baseline
  is reachable without the AI surface stealing focus.

I4 zero egress:
  The handler is wrapped with ai.GuardedHandler(`mqtt-sse-
  inspector-explanations`); when ai_mode='off' the guard returns
  HTTP 404 before any provider port is touched. The strategy
  routes every provider call through redactadapter.Wrap with
  PolicyChatbot, the rate-limit decorator, the cost-cap
  decorator, the audit decorator, and the trace decorator in the
  F10 locked order. There is no shadow path, background job,
  push channel, or service-worker chunk that bypasses the
  guard.

I5 hidden UI:
  AIMqttSseInspectorExplanations is wrapped with
  withAiFeature('mqtt-sse-inspector-explanations', InnerSection)
  which returns null when (!ai_mode_enabled || !feature_enabled).
  The off-mode React test asserts `container.toBeEmptyDOMElement()`
  for the standalone component AND asserts
  `queryByTestId('ai-feature-mqtt-sse-inspector-explanations-root')`
  is not in the DOM after mounting the full page — the wrapping
  div carrying that testid is the gate's only painted child.

I6 404 routes:
  TestMqttSseInspectorAIOffShowsRawInspectorOnly in
  internal/api/ai_mqtt_sse_inspector_explanations_handler_test.go
  proves POST /api/v1/ai/system/streams/explain returns 404 when
  ai_mode='off' AND the baseline GET /api/v1/telemetry continues
  to serve the broker-status envelope from the same router.

I7 per-feature:
  Registry entry NeedsRAG:true, NeedsTools:true, NeedsStream:true
  with explicit dependency declarations; the React off-mode test
  asserts the surface is absent EVEN when the per-feature toggle
  is on AND ai_mode='off' (proving mode > toggle), AND when
  ai_mode='cloud' AND toggle='false' (proving toggle is required
  on top of mode).

I8 propose-only:
  The strategy has NO write tools. Both registered tools
  (query_stream_inspector, retrieve_stream_chunks) are read-only.
  The handler's only write is to the SSE response stream;
  internal write paths (signal_log, snapshots, vehicle state)
  are physically unreachable from the strategy because the tool
  registration omits any writer interface.

I10 type system:
  The handler request DTO (parseMqttSseInspectorExplanationsRequest)
  validates from_unix > 0, to_unix > from_unix, window <= 24h,
  from_unix < year 2100. The body parser enforces 16 KiB max body.
  The frontend request body uses the same field names
  ({from_unix, to_unix}) so the on-mode wiring test can assert
  the exact JSON payload against the handler's expected shape.

I12 client/bg:
  No background jobs, no push kinds, no service-worker chunks,
  no client-side storage keys added by this slice. Registry
  entry JobNames=[], PushKinds=[]; aivet enforces these are
  explicit (empty slice, not nil).

P1 provider port:
  Strategy never imports a provider adapter directly. The
  dispatcher is constructed at the router level with the
  cached provider port and passed to the handler.

P4 strategy/dispatcher loop:
  Handler delegates to strategy.NewStrategy() which is
  consumed by dispatch.Run() in the standard pattern — same
  control-flow as log-trace-summarization.

P5 decorator chain:
  redactadapter.Wrap (PolicyChatbot, ModeRedactedTags,
  Allow:nil) is applied to the provider port BEFORE the
  rate-limit / cost-cap / audit / trace decorators are layered
  on. The order matches the F10 locked chain.

P6 backend guard + frontend gate:
  Backend: ai.GuardedHandler wraps the route in ai_routes.go.
  Frontend: withAiFeature HOC + useAiEnabled.

P8 eval goldens:
  3 deterministic goldens shipped (typical_healthy_streams,
  typical_stale_streams, refusal_out_of_scope_request) with
  canned mock-provider responses; `go run ./cmd/ai-eval
  --feature mqtt-sse-inspector-explanations` reports 3/3 pass.

P9 feature registry:
  Entry registered with Tier:`S6`, Name, Description, DefaultOn:
  false, NeedsRAG/Tools/Stream:true, and explicit Routes (all
  five sub-fields populated; JobNames/PushKinds as []string{}).

P10 baseline coexistence:
  The AI surface is an additive opt-in panel; the baseline
  inspector remains canonical when ai_mode='off' (proven by the
  React off-mode test) AND when ai_mode='cloud' with the toggle
  off (proven by the negative-control assertion).

P11/P12 wired-or-absent + no-placeholder-buttons (W1 inline):
  The component uses useAiStream at the top of the body (no
  early-return above the hook), the button's `disabled` is
  computed from `!canStart` and the streaming state by
  AIFeatureCard, double-submit is guarded both by the visual
  disabled and the hook's runningRef, and the placeholder
  string scan reports 0 hits in the component file.

HX scaffold:
  The component renders through AIFeatureCard with
  buttonLabel="Explain streams" (the per-feature verb, NOT
  "Ask Helix"). The accessible name reads "Ask Helix · Explain
  streams"; the on-mode wiring test uses the unanchored regex
  `/Explain streams/i`. HelixMark is rendered automatically by
  the card (not via lucide Bot). AIThinkingDots streams inside
  the button label automatically.

